WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.946
Water is a map problem before it is a numbers
problem —

2
00:00:04.066 --> 00:00:09.226
what your neighbour's well is doing matters to
yours, and so does where the rain fell.

3
00:00:09.346 --> 00:00:13.066
MyWell has two maps, and they work the same
way.

4
00:00:13.883 --> 00:00:16.691
Now we're on: My station map.

5
00:00:16.811 --> 00:00:19.811
A map of just the stations you look after.

6
00:00:19.931 --> 00:00:26.123
Tap any pin to see its latest reading, and use the
filters along the top to focus on one type,

7
00:00:26.243 --> 00:00:28.043
or one station.

8
00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:30.866
Your monitoring areas.

9
00:00:30.986 --> 00:00:34.202
A monitoring area is a saved set of stations.

10
00:00:34.322 --> 00:00:39.842
Open My Monitoring Areas to switch between
“All stations” and any area you've saved,

11
00:00:39.962 --> 00:00:42.338
or the built-in Example area.

12
00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:44.926
Filter by type.

13
00:00:45.046 --> 00:00:52.150
Open Station type to show or hide each kind of
station — groundwater wells, rainfall, check-dams,

14
00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:54.046
rivers and more.

15
00:00:54.166 --> 00:00:56.518
It doubles as the map legend.

16
00:00:57.350 --> 00:00:59.630
Find specific stations.

17
00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:05.846
Use Station to search by name or code and pick just
the stations you want; the map narrows to them.

18
00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:08.426
Build an area.

19
00:01:08.546 --> 00:01:14.594
Actions is how you create an area: Pick
stations one by one, Draw an area on the map,

20
00:01:14.714 --> 00:01:17.594
or Select area by dragging a box.

21
00:01:17.714 --> 00:01:21.002
Save it and it appears in My Monitoring Areas.

22
00:01:21.817 --> 00:01:24.745
Now we're on: Stations on map.

23
00:01:24.865 --> 00:01:27.529
Every shared station in one place.

24
00:01:27.649 --> 00:01:34.345
Filter, search, group stations into Monitoring Areas, and
read a chart of whatever the map is showing.

25
00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:37.166
Your monitoring areas.

26
00:01:37.286 --> 00:01:40.502
A monitoring area is a saved set of stations.

27
00:01:40.622 --> 00:01:46.142
Open My Monitoring Areas to switch between
“All stations” and any area you've saved,

28
00:01:46.262 --> 00:01:48.638
or the built-in Example area.

29
00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:51.226
Filter by type.

30
00:01:51.346 --> 00:01:58.450
Open Station type to show or hide each kind of
station — groundwater wells, rainfall, check-dams,

31
00:01:58.570 --> 00:02:00.346
rivers and more.

32
00:02:00.466 --> 00:02:02.818
It doubles as the map legend.

33
00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:05.930
Find specific stations.

34
00:02:06.050 --> 00:02:12.146
Use Station to search by name or code and pick just
the stations you want; the map narrows to them.

35
00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:14.726
Build an area.

36
00:02:14.846 --> 00:02:20.894
Actions is how you create an area: Pick
stations one by one, Draw an area on the map,

37
00:02:21.014 --> 00:02:23.894
or Select area by dragging a box.

38
00:02:24.014 --> 00:02:27.302
Save it and it appears in My Monitoring Areas.

39
00:02:28.117 --> 00:02:30.061
That is the whole page.

40
00:02:30.181 --> 00:02:34.837
You can replay this tutorial any time from the
Learning page inside the app.

41
00:02:34.957 --> 00:02:37.621
Thanks for helping look after our water.
